---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 5, 2026';
---

<StaticPage
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How BaggageGear collects, uses, and protects information when you visit our site."
	icon="🔒"
>
	<p class="updated" style="margin-top:-1rem;">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

	<p>
		At <strong>BaggageGear</strong>, your privacy is a top priority. This Privacy Policy outlines how we
		<strong>collect, use, and protect your personal information</strong> when you visit our website, interact
		with our content, or use our services. By using BaggageGear, you consent to the practices described in this
		Privacy Policy.
	</p>

	<h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
	<p>
		BaggageGear may collect <strong>both personal and non-personal information</strong> to improve your
		experience and provide better services.
	</p>

	<h3>Personal information</h3>
	<p>Personal information is any data that can identify you. Examples include:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Name</li>
		<li>Email address</li>
		<li>Contact information (phone number, address)</li>
		<li>Billing and payment details (if you make purchases through affiliate links)</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We collect this information <strong>only when you voluntarily provide it</strong>, such as when subscribing
		to newsletters, submitting forms, or contacting us.
	</p>

	<h3>Non-personal information</h3>
	<p>Non-personal information does not identify you directly and may include:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Browser type and version</li>
		<li>Operating system and device type</li>
		<li>IP address</li>
		<li>Pages visited and time spent on the site</li>
		<li>Referral website or search engine used</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		This information is collected automatically using cookies, analytics tools, and server logs to help us
		improve our website.
	</p>

	<h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
	<p>We use the information we collect for purposes including:</p>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Providing Services:</strong> Delivering content, product reviews, guides, and recommendations tailored to your interests.</li>
		<li><strong>Improving the Website:</strong> Analyzing usage patterns, optimizing content, and enhancing site functionality.</li>
		<li><strong>Communication:</strong> Sending newsletters, updates, promotional content, or responding to inquiries.</li>
		<li><strong>Affiliate Transactions:</strong> Processing purchases made through affiliate links and ensuring accurate commission tracking (see our <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a> page).</li>
		<li><strong>Legal Compliance:</strong> Ensuring compliance with applicable laws and regulations.</li>
	</ol>
	<p>We <strong>do not sell or rent your personal information</strong> to third parties.</p>

	<h2>3. Cookies and tracking technologies</h2>
	<p>
		BaggageGear uses <strong>cookies and similar technologies</strong> to improve your browsing experience and
		track website performance.
	</p>
	<h3>Types of cookies</h3>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Essential Cookies:</strong> Required for website functionality, such as navigation and secure areas.</li>
		<li><strong>Performance Cookies:</strong> Track user interactions to analyze website usage and improve content.</li>
		<li><strong>Functional Cookies:</strong> Remember your preferences, such as language or location settings.</li>
		<li><strong>Advertising/Targeting Cookies:</strong> Display relevant ads based on browsing behavior (used with third-party services).</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		You can manage or disable cookies through your browser settings. However, some website features may not
		function properly if cookies are disabled.
	</p>

	<h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
	<p>BaggageGear may use third-party services, including:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Affiliate networks</strong> (Amazon Associates, etc.)</li>
		<li><strong>Advertising partners</strong> (Google AdSense, etc.)</li>
		<li><strong>Analytics tools</strong> (Google Analytics, etc.)</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		These third parties may collect and use information as described in their own privacy policies. BaggageGear
		<strong>does not control third-party practices</strong> and encourages users to review their privacy
		policies.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Email communications</h2>
	<p>If you subscribe to BaggageGear newsletters or updates, we may send emails containing:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Blog posts, product reviews, and guides</li>
		<li>Promotional offers or affiliate recommendations</li>
		<li>Updates about our website and services</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		You can <strong>unsubscribe at any time</strong> using the link in our emails. We respect your preferences and
		will promptly remove your email from our mailing list upon request.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Data security</h2>
	<p>
		We implement <strong>reasonable security measures</strong> to protect your personal information from
		unauthorized access, disclosure, or alteration. These measures include:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Secure server environments</li>
		<li>Encryption for sensitive data (where applicable)</li>
		<li>Regular monitoring of security systems</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		While we strive to protect your information, no website or online service is completely secure. By using
		BaggageGear, you acknowledge that <strong>we cannot guarantee absolute security</strong> of your data.
	</p>

	<h2>7. Children's privacy</h2>
	<p>
		BaggageGear is <strong>not directed to children under 13</strong>. We do not knowingly collect personal
		information from children.
	</p>
	<p>
		If we become aware that a child has provided personal information without parental consent, we will
		<strong>take steps to remove such information immediately</strong>.
	</p>
	<p>Parents or guardians can contact us if they believe their child has submitted personal data.</p>

	<h2>8. Third-party links</h2>
	<p>
		BaggageGear may contain links to <strong>third-party websites</strong>, including online stores, travel
		services, and affiliate partners.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>These third parties may have their own privacy policies.</li>
		<li>BaggageGear is <strong>not responsible for the privacy practices</strong> of any external sites.</li>
		<li>Users should review the privacy policies of any website they visit via our links.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>9. User rights and control</h2>
	<p>You have the right to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
		<li>Request corrections or updates to your information</li>
		<li>Request deletion of your personal data</li>
		<li>Opt-out of marketing communications</li>
	</ul>
	<p>To exercise these rights, please <strong>contact us directly</strong> via our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>

	<h2>10. Legal compliance and disclosure</h2>
	<p>
		BaggageGear may disclose personal information when required by law or in response to legal requests,
		including:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Compliance with laws, regulations, or legal processes</li>
		<li>Protecting rights, property, or safety of our website, users, or others</li>
		<li>Investigating fraud, security breaches, or violations of our <a href="/terms/">Terms</a></li>
	</ul>

	<h2>11. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
	<p>
		BaggageGear may <strong>update this Privacy Policy</strong> from time to time to reflect changes in
		practices, legal requirements, or services.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Updates will be posted on this page with the revised "Last updated" date.</li>
		<li>Continued use of the website after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>We encourage users to <strong>review this Privacy Policy periodically</strong> to stay informed.</p>

	<h2>12. Contact us</h2>
	<p>
		If you have questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy, please reach out to us via our
		<a href="/contact/"><strong>Contact Page</strong></a>.
	</p>
	<p>We are committed to addressing your privacy concerns and responding to inquiries promptly.</p>
</StaticPage>
